        "id": 158849,
        "name": "Matchstickman",
        "username": "Matchstickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-04T22:38:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>mwc146 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I do remember Chris or someone saying that the Argent Adept is unusual among the Virtuosos of the Void for having to fight Akash'Bhuta repeatedly -- usually, she goes dormant for a while after being fought once.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI forget who said it, but it was in reference to the appearance of Akash'Dharsha in the Tactics time-frame. So Akhash'Bhuta would only appear once during the time covered by SotM. (Although it's likely she fought more than one hero team during that one appearance.)\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Me. <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/111926#comment-111926\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Here</a></p>",
